findings.description:
The agents install writes skill directories into a shared root, then writes a receipt. The design says only that nothing is written when validation fails. It does not say what happens when:
- a write fails partway through (permissions, full disk), leaving files with no receipt;
- the receipt write fails after the files are written;
- a recorded file is already gone, or a recorded path fails the containment check, during `remove_receipt_files`;
- a receipt is missing, unreadable, or corrupt on uninstall or list;
- a SKILL.md is missing, unparseable, or unreadable (D3 lists rules, not these).

None of these has a stated handling, a signal (exit code or WARNING), or a test. The Technical Requirements (line 233) include no write or removal failure test. The GitHub clone that `--ide codex` now reaches (line 92) inherits its failure behavior without comment. The project's failure-mode rule (`review-code.md`) requires each new I/O path to name its partial-failure behavior and make it observable. Document the write ordering (receipt before or after files, and cleanup on failure), the signal for each case, and a test for each.

Plan Part A (`900-slices…md:454`) covers `--ide` on `skills install` and `skills uninstall`. The 925 entry describes #125 as "`sq skills install --ide`" (line 430). This slice also adds:
- `skills list --ide` (criterion 4);
- per-target doctor rows (D8, criterion 5);
- a `PACK_LAYOUTS.installed_path` table (D6), whose only callers are list and doctor;
- `--local` on skills, for parity with 925 (not in the plan);
- the `sq model list` fix (found while probing).

The Overview ties list and doctor to #125. I have not checked the issue text. Plan line 457 records the rule-file and doctor-rule decisions but not these additions. Either amend the plan entry to name each addition, or move list, doctor, and `installed_path` to a follow-up and say so.
